 "_doc": "Sidebar screen -> the GET endpoints it loads when it opens, and the permissions that let a person open it. A sidebar item is shown when the signed-in person holds one of `perms` organisation- or platform-wide; `perms` is the intersection of what the backend guards of every listed read accept, so a visible item never answers 403 on load. Screens without reads (self-service or static) have no `perms` and are always shown to their personas. Navigation only: the backend authorises every request. `reads` is maintained by hand; `perms` is generated from the backend operation registry and checked by backend/tests/test_sidebar_integration.py. `shell` lists the header and sidebar-footer reads every page makes (record watermark, alert counts, entity scope); they are made only for someone holding one of their `perms`, so a page view never records a refusal. `panels` lists in-page panels that are shown only to people holding one of their `perms` (for example the Team & Access directory and role registry).",
 "_generated_by": "python tests/test_sidebar_integration.py  (from backend/)",
